            {
                "entry_id": "b482ecbe-48b6-3a6c-89b8-ed638954d155",
                "word": "exceptionnalisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "15736fc0-6f99-412f-91e7-d293a2913fc2",
                        "entry_id": "b482ecbe-48b6-3a6c-89b8-ed638954d155",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "exceptionnalismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "534fee69-1964-3129-bba8-db3e2bd1fd9a",
                        "entry_id": "b482ecbe-48b6-3a6c-89b8-ed638954d155",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Perception ou croyance selon laquelle une espèce, un pays, une société, une institution, un mouvement, un individu ou une période de temps est \\\"exceptionnel\\\". Le terme implique que le référent est supérieur d'une manière ou d'une autre, que ce soit spécifié ou non."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42c42586-8c23-429d-b3fa-efc28c4e2f12",
                                "sense_id": "534fee69-1964-3129-bba8-db3e2bd1fd9a",
                                "text": "Chose certaine, pour propager l’image d’une Russie de retour sur la scène internationale, d’une nation triomphante, d’un pays encore habité par le sentiment de l’exceptionnalisme slave et de la supériorité morale, le maître du Kremlin n’a pas lésiné sur les moyens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb498c67-399f-4bf4-8aa5-37b8d79a1819",
                                "sense_id": "534fee69-1964-3129-bba8-db3e2bd1fd9a",
                                "text": "La supériorité morale inhérente des Américains blancs est l’un des préceptes fondamentaux de l’exceptionnalisme américain. La présidence de Trump dont l’électorat est constitué à 57 % de blancs a su manipuler à son avantage ce mythe prétentieux."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ebfc6fe1-8098-4470-a6c1-bf046858c31a",
                        "source_entry_id": "b482ecbe-48b6-3a6c-89b8-ed638954d155",
                        "source_sense_id": "534fee69-1964-3129-bba8-db3e2bd1fd9a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Exzeptionalismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "98c998d6-d397-4efb-96e1-d4ee8bb84800",
                        "source_entry_id": "b482ecbe-48b6-3a6c-89b8-ed638954d155",
                        "source_sense_id": "534fee69-1964-3129-bba8-db3e2bd1fd9a",
                        "target_lang_word": "exceptionalism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exceptionalism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e78814f-b95d-320b-886c-f4cb55512642",
                                        "entry_id": "baefd102-baf3-3cdd-87a1-7b9ed3b25399",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being special, exceptional or unique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a7f582e-1b7d-37ff-9a7d-e2fe99648cca",
                                        "entry_id": "baefd102-baf3-3cdd-87a1-7b9ed3b25399",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The belief that something (a nation, species etc.) is exceptional, superior, or does not conform to an established norm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b9e6aaa-2f1e-40c8-b5fb-1d079d523945",
                                                "sense_id": "7a7f582e-1b7d-37ff-9a7d-e2fe99648cca",
                                                "text": "If Covid-19 eventually imbues human beings with some humility, it’s possible that we will, after all, be receptive to the lessons of this lethal pandemic. Or perhaps we will sink back into our culture of complacent exceptionalism and await the next plague that will surely arrive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "538a8a24-6bf2-4a62-9227-a314479d5443",
                                                "sense_id": "7a7f582e-1b7d-37ff-9a7d-e2fe99648cca",
                                                "text": "“This is a moment of American exceptionalism,” Jen Psaki, the White House press secretary, said when asked about the flight during a Tuesday news conference."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48298606-fb76-4dd8-afb0-23467db41614",
                                                "sense_id": "7a7f582e-1b7d-37ff-9a7d-e2fe99648cca",
                                                "text": "But in fact the antinomy of exceptionalism and assimilationism has been there all along, and otherwise puzzling decisions from the nineteenth and twentieth centuries become readily understandable when seen as moments when assimilationism was ascendant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38802b91-b06e-3943-ba31-116259a71b03",
                                        "entry_id": "baefd102-baf3-3cdd-87a1-7b9ed3b25399",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A philosophy of prevention or of intervention."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f4c4f73-b430-411f-beeb-0b53ac99a416",
                        "source_entry_id": "b482ecbe-48b6-3a6c-89b8-ed638954d155",
                        "source_sense_id": "534fee69-1964-3129-bba8-db3e2bd1fd9a",
                        "target_lang_word": "excepcionalismo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
